 "title": "Пари на кухне  (A Bet in the Kitchen)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "max": "Макс"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Max proudly shows off his festive dessert, and the guest who is supposed to taste it turns out to be Eleonora Andreyevna, a dog. She won't even look at it. Max is furious at the unfairness, and ends up challenging the chef to a bet. Here is the Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, праздничный десерт уже готов!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Все внимание! Гостья пробует блюдо новичка.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Иди сюда, милая собачка! Попробуй десерт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Она даже не смотрит на тарелку.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, это нечестно! Это же собака.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Мир вообще не идеален, молодой человек.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Давайте поспорим, шеф!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "О чём мы будем спорить?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Обычному человеку понравится моё горячее блюдо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Хорошо! Ты приготовишь блюдо для меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Если мне понравится, ты остаёшься здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Если нет, ты уйдёшь отсюда навсегда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я согласен на этот спор!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Посмотрим, какой из тебя повар!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Back to the kitchen, slowly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, праздничный десерт уже готов!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, the festive dessert is already ready!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Праздничный",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " comes from the word for a holiday. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Уже готов",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"already ready\", which sounds clumsy in English but perfectly normal in Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Все внимание! Гостья пробует блюдо новичка.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Attention everyone! The guest is tasting the newcomer's dish.' A woman guest is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "гостья",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the same word with a feminine ending. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Блюдо новичка",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"dish of newcomer\", with a short \"of\" ending on the word for newcomer and no 's.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Иди сюда, милая собачка! Попробуй десерт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Come here, sweet little doggy! Taste the dessert.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The word for doggy is the word for dog with a small ending that makes it a pet name. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Милая",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"sweet\", the feminine of the word for sweet. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Попробуй",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is a command from the verb to try.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Она даже не смотрит на тарелку.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She doesn't even look at the plate.' A dog is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "она",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", she, because the word for doggy is a feminine word. The verb means \"to look at\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "тарелку",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " takes -u.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, это нечестно! Это же собака.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, that is unfair! After all, it is a dog.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Нечестно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "не",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " plus ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "честно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", honestly, the word from \"frankly speaking\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Это же собака",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " has the ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "же",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " for \"after all\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Мир вообще не идеален, молодой человек.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The world is not ideal at all, young man.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Мир",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means both \"world\" and \"peace\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Идеален",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the short form of the word for ideal, the shape Russian uses after \"is\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Давайте поспорим, шеф!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let's make a bet, chef!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Давайте",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"give\", but before another verb it means \"let's\", and it's one of the most useful words in Russian. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Поспорим",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " comes from ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "спор",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", an argument or bet.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "О чём мы будем спорить?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What will we bet about?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "О чём",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"about what\", as before. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Мы будем спорить",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"we will bet\", the future \"will be\" plus \"to bet\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Обычному человеку понравится моё горячее блюдо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'An ordinary person will like my hot dish.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Обычному человеку",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"to an ordinary person\", both words with the \"to\" ending, because the person is the one pleased. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Горячее",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"hot\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Хорошо! Ты приготовишь блюдо для меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Good! You will prepare a dish for me.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Для меня",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"for me\". Where English has one \"me\", Russian has several forms, and this is the \"for\" one.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Если мне понравится, ты остаёшься здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'If I like it, you stay here.' Russian turns liking around: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "мне понравится",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"it will please me\", so the dish is the subject and Barinov is \"to me\". Then ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "остаёшься",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", you stay, is in the present, which makes the promise sound settled.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Если нет, ты уйдёшь отсюда навсегда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'If not, you will leave here forever.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Навсегда",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "на",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " plus ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "всегда",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", always: forever. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Отсюда",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"from here\", the partner of ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "сюда",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", \"to here\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я согласен на этот спор!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I agree to this bet!' A man says ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "согласен",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", and a woman would use a different ending. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "На этот спор",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"to this bet\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Посмотрим, какой из тебя повар!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We will see what kind of cook you are!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Посмотрим",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is \"we will see\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Какой из тебя повар",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is literally \"what from you cook\", Russian for \"what kind of cook you'll turn out to be\". Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, праздничный десерт уже готов!",
   "gap": 0.5
